{"conversation":"Oh, I see. So if multiple tasks have the same maximum count, they also need to be spaced out, which reduces the number of idle slots we can use for other tasks. I need to calculate how many tasks have this max_count and account for that in the formula by multiplying blocks with (n + 1) and then adding the number of max count tasks at the end.","python_code":"from collections import Counter

class Solution:
    def leastInterval(self, tasks: List[str], n: int) -> int:
        task_counts = Counter(tasks)
        max_count = max(task_counts.values())
        max_count_tasks = list(task_counts.values()).count(max_count)
